# ui/ and app/: Qt code. Inherits the root config (coding-standards.md section 7 Qt rules) minus two checks:
#   cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory   Qt parent-child ownership: `new QWidget(parent)` is the idiom, the parent deletes
#   bugprone-exception-escape         Qt slots and lambdas connected to signals cannot propagate exceptions anyway, and
#                                     core/ui never throw (section 4); the check fires on every std::string capture
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -bugprone-exception-escape
